From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HeDo <ldileo@digipa.it>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:57:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] OutStream::push does nothing for an empty array

It called memcpy(pos, b, 0) for an empty array, and an empty BitStream (one that nothing was
written to) has a null buffer: memcpy with a null source is undefined even when it copies no
byte (UBSan: "null pointer passed as argument 2, which is declared to never be null"). Nothing
is added to the stream for an empty array, so the output does not change.
---
 include/corto/cstream.h | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/corto/cstream.h b/include/corto/cstream.h
index 54c79ed..71cf935 100644
--- a/include/corto/cstream.h
+++ b/include/corto/cstream.h
@@ -97,6 +97,8 @@ public:
 	}
 
 	void push(const void *b, size_t s) {
+		if(s == 0)
+			return;
 		uchar *pos = grow(s);
 		memcpy(pos, b, s);
 	}
